      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\), we multiply the numerators together and the denominators together. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Identify the numerators and denominators of the fractions.\n   - The numerator of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) is \\(1\\).\n   - The numerator of \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(3\\).\n   - The denominator of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) is \\(5\\).\n   - The denominator of \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(7\\).\n\n2. Multiply the numerators together.\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 3 = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply the denominators together.\n   \\[\n   5 \\times 7 = 35\n   \\]\n\n4. Combine the results to form the new fraction.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1}{5} \\times \\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3}{35}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of \\(\\frac{1}{5}\\) and \\(\\frac{3}{7}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{3}{35}}\\).",
